This folder contains checks for the sane operation of the submission/processing
infrastructure, particularly in networked mode and with respect to widely varying
calculation times. It runs a Go2 optimization of GDelayIndividual (whose
"evaluation" simply sleeps for configurable durations) and can log the timings
of all processing steps via --monitorTimings.

measureIterationTime.sh measures, with a server and N clients on one host, how
long an iteration takes and how much CPU the server needs for it; with
individuals that only sleep, the time above the sleep is what the submission
infrastructure and the transport add. summarizeIterationTimes.py turns its
result lines into a table. Both describe their arguments in their header. Run
them from a work directory outside the source tree.
